I fixed #1083 in commit dc2349ce. Pushing it will close the issue.

What changed (only src/commands_dev.rs, which went from 1921 to 1952 lines, still under the 2,000-line limit):
• I added curl_row_detail(surface, found), written the same way as the two per-surface helpers from #1075. The Curl check now uses it.
• The Curl line in the REPL /doctor is unchanged.
• Shell yoyo doctor now prints:
  ```
  ✓ Curl: installed (for yoyo docs, and /web inside a session)
  ⚠ Curl: not found (yoyo docs and the in-session /web won't work)
  ```
  I saw both lines in a real run; the second one with PATH=/nonexistent so curl couldn't be found.

Tests: A new test checks all four cases (each surface, curl found or not). The REPL text must match the old wording exactly, and the shell text must mention yoyo docs and must not contain /docs. To make sure the test can fail, I put the REPL wording back into the shell case: the test failed, and passed again once I restored it. Formatting, clippy and the full test suite all pass.

Left over: git grep '#1083' found nothing. But yoyo help doctor, run from the shell, still prints the /doctor help text, including "Curl — needed for /docs and /web". That's the broader problem of help text showing REPL slash commands on the shell, which #1086 already tracks. Since this push closes #1083, I added that case to #1086 as a comment rather than filing a new issue, with the line number and the commit it was checked against.
